==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|vitlauss}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*witjalausaz}}, whence also {{cog|en|witless}}. Composed of {{suffix|is|vit|gloss1=wits, intellect|laus|gloss2=[[-less]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈvɪht.løyːs/}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|vitlausari|vitlausastur}}

# [[stupid]], [[foolish]]
#: ''Mikið eru [[dúfa|dúfur]] '''vitlaus''' dýr.''
#:: Pigeons are such '''stupid''' animals.
# {{lb|is|informal}} [[insane]], [[crazy]]
#: ''Er allt orðið '''vitlaust''' hérna?''
#:: Has everything gone '''mad''' here?
# {{lb|is|colloquial}} [[wrong]], [[incorrect]]
#: ''Þetta svar er '''vitlaust'''.''
#:: This answer is '''wrong'''.

